# 5. The most important part: run the Action

After committing `snake.yml`:

Go to:

```text
YOUR_USERNAME repository
        ↓
Actions
        ↓
Generate Contribution Snake
        ↓
Run workflow
        ↓
Run workflow
```

The workflow has `workflow_dispatch`, so it can be started manually, in addition to its daily scheduled run. ([GitHub][5])

The workflow's `contents: write` permission allows it to publish the generated SVGs into the `output` branch using the repository's built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN`; no personal access token is required for this same-repository setup. The deployment action documents `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `target_branch`/`build_dir` usage. ([GitHub][4])

---

